 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "There are, but on the top of a mountain,\nNot more than the size which we can afford\nTo send our paces to or our\nPuns back. - Let them down; they'll work themselves,\nAnd I'll be content - No doubt I cannot\nMake out their purpose if I cannot\nDisguise myself in idle jests again.\nSuch things as these will do no harm indeed\nIn America: and this is our\nRule! A man needs his self (so far indeed\nHe does), he calls it 'the soul' within\nThat which consists of all that's within",
